<h1>{title}</h1>

<p class="lead">The everyday word for <strong>help</strong> in Marathi is <strong>मदत</strong> (madat) — feminine, from Hindi/Urdu. The formal Sanskrit equivalent is <strong>सहाय्य</strong> (sahāyy). This guide covers both, plus emergency phrases you need to recognize.</p>

<h2>Quick Answer</h2>
<table class="vocab-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Marathi</th><th>Transliteration</th><th>Context</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>मदत</td><td>madat</td><td>Help (everyday, feminine)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>सहाय्य</td><td>sahāyy</td><td>Assistance (formal, official)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>मदत करा</td><td>madat karā</td><td>Help me / Please help (imperative)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>मला मदत पाहिजे</td><td>malā madat pāhije</td><td>I need help</td></tr>
    <tr><td>मदत हवा?</td><td>madat havā?</td><td>Do you need help?</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Grammar: मदत is Feminine</h2>
<p>मदत ends in त but is feminine (like चहा, भाषा). Possessives and adjectives agree:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>माझी मदत</strong> — My help</li>
  <li><strong>तिची मदत</strong> — Her help</li>
  <li><strong>मदत करणे</strong> — To help (verb phrase, neuter infinitive)</li>
</ul>
<div class="tip-box"><strong>Tip:</strong> मदत is a noun. The verb is <strong>मदत करणे</strong> (to help). <em>तो मला मदत करतो</em> = He helps me. <em>मी तो मदत करतो</em> = I help him.</div>

<h2>Everyday vs Emergency</h2>
<table class="vocab-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Marathi</th><th>Tone</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Can you help me?</td><td>तु मला मदत करशील का?</td><td>Polite request</td></tr>
    <tr><td>I need help</td><td>मला मदत पाहिजे</td><td>Direct need</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Help! (emergency)</td><td>मदत! / बचवा!</td><td>Urgent — बचवा = save me</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Call for help</td><td>मदत सांगा / पोलिसांना फोन करा</td><td>Emergency action</td></tr>
    <tr><td>First aid</td><td>प्राथमिक उपचार</td><td>Medical term</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Helpline</td><td>मदत नंबर / हेल्पलाइन</td><td>Phone number</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>सहाय्य vs मदत</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>मदत</strong> — Daily life: <em>मदत करा</em>, <em>मदत पाहिजे</em>, <em>मदत नंबर</em></li>
  <li><strong>सहाय्य</strong> — Official/formal: <em>सरकारी सहाय्य</em> (govt assistance), <em>आर्थिक सहाय्य</em> (financial aid), <em>सहाय्य केंद्र</em> (help center)</li>
</ul>

<h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>❌ माझा मदत</strong> → <strong>✅ माझी मदत</strong> (feminine)</li>
  <li><strong>❌ मदत करो</strong> → <strong>✅ मदत करा</strong> (Marathi imperative ends in -आ, not -ओ)</li>
  <li><strong>❌ हेल्प</strong> → Use <strong>मदत</strong> or <strong>सहाय्य</strong></li>
</ul>

<h2>Mini Practice</h2>
<ol>
  <li>"I need help" → <em>मला मदत पाहिजे</em></li>
  <li>"Please help me" → <em>मला मदत करा</em></li>
  <li>"Help! (emergency)" → <em>मदत! / बचवा!</em></li>
</ol>

